      "sourceText": "USAFRICOM TRAVEL MEDICAL SCREENING CHECKLIST\nTRAVELER WILL RETAIN AND PROVIDE THIS COMPLETED FORM WHENEVER SEEKING TRAVEL CLEARANCE TO THE AFRICOM AOR.\nSCREENING IS VALID FOR 120 DAYS FROM PROVIDER SIGNATURE DATE IN PART I/*.\nPART I: TRAVELER'S DATA & PERSONAL HEALTH TRAVEL REQUIREMENTS (COMPLETED BY TRAVELER)\nNAME: LAST, FIRST, MI\nGRADE\nUNIT / DUTY PHONE\nTRAVEL DESTINATION(S) & DATES:\nPRIOR TO ENTRY INTO THE AFRICOM AOR (TRAVELER READ & INITIAL EACH BOX)\nI WILL NOTIFY MY PROVIDER OF MY TRAVEL DESTINATION(S); I WILL OBTAIN\nIF I BECOME ILL WITHIN A YEAR AFTER TRAVELING TO THE USAFRICOM AOR, I\nSUFFICIENT QUANTITIES OF PRESCRIBED ANTI-MALARIAL MEDICATION; AND I WILL\nUNDERSTAND I AM TO SEEK MEDICAL ATTENTION AND INFORM MEDICAL PERSONNEL THAT\nI HAVE TRAVELED TO AFRICA.\nI HAVE ON-HAND SUFFICIENT QUANTITIES OF MY OTHER CURRENTLY PRESCRIBED\nI HAVE REVIEWED THE GENERAL HEALTH COUNSELING BRIEFING AT: GENERAL\nMEDICATION(S) AND/OR MEDICAL EQUIPMENT.\nHEALTH COUNSELING\nI HAVE OBTAINED INSECT REPELLENT CONTAINING DEET, PICARIDIN, OR IR3535 AND\nI HAVE ENROLLED IN THE DEPARTMENT OF STATE SMART TRAVELER\nWILL USE TO PREVENT INSECT BITES.\nI HAVE SUFFICIENT CLOTHING/UNIFORMS/BEDNETS/ TREATED WITH PERMETHRIN\n(INSECT REPELLENT) FOR THE DURATION OF TRAVEL IF DEPLOYING OR GOING TDY TO\nLA FIELD SETTING\nI HAVE REVIEWED THE ELECTRONIC FOREIGN CLEARANCE GUIDE (EFCG), SECTIONS\n1.A/B.3.b.5 MEDICAL ASSESSMENT AND 1.C.2 HEALTH, MEDICAL ALERTS,\nIMMUNIZATIONS FOR EACH COUNTRY TO BE VISITED:\nI UNDERSTAND I AM NOT TO SWIM IN BODIES OF FRESH WATER OR SEA WATER\nUNLESS APPROVED BY APPROPRIATE AUTHORITIES, AND IF EXPOSED TO FRESH\nWATER, I WILL DRY OFF IMMEDIATELY.\nI UNDERSTAND I AM NOT TO PHYSICALLY CONTACT, KEEP OR FEED ANY ANIMALS IN\nTHE AFRICOM AOR.\nCIVILIANS/CONTRACTORS (including retired military): I UNDERSTAND THAT I MAY NOT\nBE SYSTEMATICALLY COVERED BY ANY FORM OF MEDICAL EVACUATION PLAN. I\nUNDERSTAND MY OPTIONS FOR MEDICAL EVACUATION OUT OF THE AFRICOM AOR.\nI HAVE REVIEWED SHORELINE TRAVAX (https://www.travax.com/) OR US CDC TRAVEL\nPLANNER (TRAVEL PLANNER) FOR COUNTRY SPECIFIC MEDICAL RISKS INCLUDING FOOD\nAND WATER-BORNE ILLNESS AS WELL AS HEALTH AND SAFETY NOTICES.\nI HAVE DISCUSSED THIS TRAVEL WITH MY HEALTH CARE PROVIDER INCLUDING ANY PROFILES\nOR DUTY LIMITING CONDITIONS.\nJNLESS EXEMPT BY ACI 4200.09 OR EFCG, I AM TRAVELING WITH A CDC FORM 73\nYELLOW SHOT CARD) STAMPED WITH AN OFFICIAL YELLOW FEVER CERTIFICATI\nPREGNANCY TEST: I HAVE DISCUSSED MY PREGNANCY STATUS WITH\nTHE MEDICAL SCREENER.\nI ACKNOWLEDGE AND HAVE MET PERSONAL MEDICAL REQUIREMENTS FOR ENTRY INTO THE AFRICOM AOR.\nTRAVELER'S SIGNATURE:\nDATE:\nPART II: MEDICAL SCREENING REQUIREMENTS (COMPLETED BY MEDICAL SCREENER)\nMEDICALLY READY IAW SERVICE OR AGENCY GUIDELINES (CONTRACTORS IAW DODI 3020.41)\n\"NO\" ANSWERS) MUST BE COMPLETED, EXEMPTED OR WAIVED (VACCINES NOT WAIVERABLE UNLESS NOT REQUIRED)\nFOR WAIVER REQUIREMENT INFORMATION, CONTACT: africom.stuttgart.acsg.mbx.j004-force-health-protection@mail.mil\nVACCINATIONS CURRENT:\nYELLOW FEVER (DOSE MUST BE AT LEAST 10 DAYS PRIOR TO ARRIVAL TO AFRICA; Review the FCG for ETP)\nTETANUS-DIPHTHERIA (EVERY 10YRS; ONE TIME ADULT BOOSTER OF TAP IF NOT PREVIOUSLY RECEIVED)\nVARICELLA (DOCUMENTED IMMUNITY OR VACCINATION)\nMEASLES, MUMPS, RUBELLA (Serologic immunity or TWO LIFETIME DOSES ARE REQUIRED if born after 1957)\nPOLIOVIRUS (SERIES COMPLETE PLUS SINGLE ADULT BOOSTER AND COUNTRY-SPECIFIC REQUIREMENTS)\nHEPATITIS A (SERIES COMPLETE OR FIRST DOSE AT LEAST 14 DAYS PRIOR TO TRAVEL\nHEPATITIS B (SERIES COMPLETE OR FIRST DOSE AT LEAST 14 DAYS PRIOR TO TRAVEL)\nMENINGOCOCCAL (EVERY 5 YRS)\nTYPHOID (INJECTABLE EVERY 2 YRS; ORAL EVERY 5YRS)\nRABIES (AS NEEDED FOR OCCUPATIONAL EXPOSURE, OTHER EXPOSURE RISK, OR HRIG UNAVAILABLE)\nPNEUMOCOCCAL (Indicated for high risk health conditions)\nCURRENT PHA / Physical (Military / Civilian)\nLAB WORK CURRENT IAW SERVICE GUIDELINES\nDENTAL CLASS 1/2 STATUS (MILITARY ONLY) / Current dental screening IAW ACI 4200.09 (Civilian)\nSCREENING FOUND NO DUTY/DEPLOYMENT-LIMITING MEDICAL CONDITION DEFINED BY ACI 4200.09\nIF NEEDED, USE AC FORM 43, MEDICAL WAIVER REQUEST: MEDICAL-WAIVER-PROCESS\nTRAVELER PRESCRIBED/ISSUED RECOMMENDED MEDICAL EQUIPMENT\nTRAVELER PRESCRIBED RECOMMENDED MEDICATIONS FOR COMMON TRAVELER ILLNESSES\nTRAVELER PRESCRIBED MALARIA CHEMOPROPHYLAXIS PER NCMI OR TRAVAX ASSESSMENT OF TRANSMISSION\nRISK: HTTPS://WWW.NCMI.DODIIS.MIL OR HTTPS://WWW.TRAVAX.COM (Note: No Chloroquine)\nPREGNANCY TEST: A NEGATIVE TEST (WITHIN 30 DAYS OF TRAVEL) FOR TRAVEL OF 30 DAYS OR MORE\nTHE TRAVELER MEETS MEDICAL SCREENING REQUIREMENTS FOR ENTRY INTO THE AFRICOM AOR PER ACI 4200.09A\nProvider SIGNATURE:\nYES\n口\nCOMMENTS\n口\nロ\n口\n•\n口\nDATE:\nAC FORM 42, 01 June 2026\nFor use of this form, see U.S. Africa Command Instruction 4200.09\nUNCLASSIFIED\n\nUNCLAS",
